{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0449","billNumberShort":"H.B. 449","billNumberLong":"HB0449","fileNumber":"2026FL0389","shortTitle":"Utah Taxpayer Oversight of Government Spending Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"AUXIET","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Auxier, Tiara","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill establishes taxpayer oversight of government spending. ","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>establishes taxpayer oversight of government spending as required by a proposed amendment to the Utah Constitution, including:<hr><ltbullet1>requiring voters to approve an increase in state or local government revenue through most taxes or government debt;<hr><ltbullet1>limiting the amount of revenue a government entity may spend in a fiscal year unless voters approve increased spending; <hr><ltbullet1>eliminating automatic increases to taxes; and<hr><ltbullet1>requiring a refund of excess revenue to taxpayers;<hr><ltbullet>repeals provisions requiring residential property to be assessed using any method other than the sales comparison approach;<hr><ltbullet>modifies elections provisions to accommodate voting requirements;<hr><ltbullet>exempts business personal property that is not subject to a uniform fee from property tax; <hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes; and<hr><ltbullet>makes these changes contingent upon passage of a proposed constitutional amendment.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Andrea Valenti Arthur","fiscalAnalyst":"Andrea Wilko","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"BUIVACKSTF","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-02 08:36:48.610","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":